# Database rules (PostgreSQL / Supabase)

- Add a new file `backend/db/migrations/NNN_short_name.sql`; `npm run db:migrate` applies each file once in a transaction.
  Never edit or reorder applied migrations. Write migrations so they also run on plain PostgreSQL 14+ (local dev, CI).
- Naming: snake_case tables/columns matching spec §14 (holiday_dialysis_request, request_status_history, …);
  uuid PKs for business records, bigserial for logs; `timestamptz` for instants, `date` for business dates.
- Controlled values are `text` + `CHECK (... IN (...))`, mirrored in `backend/src/domain/constants.js` — change both together.
- Append-only tables (audit_event, request_status_history, request_decision, provider_communication, generated_letter)
  have triggers that reject UPDATE/DELETE. Corrections are new rows.
- Only Draft requests can be deleted; statuses can never return to Draft; terminal statuses can't change (triggers in 002).
- **Supabase REST lockdown:** every table in `public` has RLS enabled with no policies, so Supabase's anon/authenticated
  REST API sees nothing. New tables must also `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` (add it in the same migration).
- The backend connects with the Supabase `postgres` role through the pooler. Use the session pooler (5432) or direct
  connection for migrations.
- Seed data lives in `seed.sql` and is development-only (fictional people, `.example` emails).
